    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the offensive upside of **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Jackson Merrill** is our strongest play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Brandon Pfaadt and a significant boost from the opposing battery\u2019s slow delivery, which positions him for a critical stolen base opportunity in a high-leverage 5x5 environment. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a high-efficiency matchup against McGreevy; his dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and favorable #3 spot in the order make him a high-floor, high-ceiling anchor for our run production today.\n\nWhile our core is set, we are navigating a few situational variables. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.86) remains a must-start despite facing a tough assignment in Cristian Javier; his high-pedigree profile overcomes the SP skill delta. Meanwhile, **Heliot Ramos** (64.37) and **Kyle Tucker** (65.36) provide reliable support, though both face specific hurdles\u2014**Heliot Ramos** deals with a pending lineup status and an SP who limits base runners, while **Kyle Tucker** must contend with a platoon disadvantage against Matthew Boyd. **Nasim Nunez** (50.95) represents our most marginal start; while he is vital for our pursuit of scarcity in the SB category, he is vulnerable against Aaron Nola, and his position at the bottom of the order tempers our expectations for run contribution. \n\nRegarding roster management, the depth of our bench remains compromised by several factors. **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jorge Polanco** are unavailable due to team off-days, while **Jordan Westburg** remains sidelined on the IL. Given the scarcity of active bats today, we are effectively forced into our current alignment, as no available reserve options\u2014such as **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, or **Sam Antonacci**\u2014offer a superior projection to our active starters. We will monitor the status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Heliot Ramos** closely, as any late-breaking lineup shifts could necessitate a pivot to our deeper reserves like **Miguel Vargas** or **Josh Jung** to maintain our daily game cap efficiency.",
